fish-research-experiments-button = Experiments
fish-research-experiments-button-hint = Practical objectives, shared progress and technology discounts.
fish-research-experiments-hint = Measure samples with the experimental scanner and produce the listed equipment on connected lathes. Using the scanner in hand opens server selection. Progress is shared by consoles of one server; only the strongest discount applies. Completing an experiment after paying for its technology refunds the price difference.
fish-research-experiments-empty = No experiments are configured.
fish-research-experiments-recipes = Accepted recipes: { $recipes }.
fish-research-experiments-progress = Progress: { $current } / { $required }
fish-research-experiments-reward = Reward: { $percent }% off { $technology }.
fish-research-experiments-show-reward = Show technology
fish-research-experiments-status-progress = Complete the experiment's conditions.
fish-research-experiments-status-completed = Experiment complete. This server can use the discount.
fish-research-experiments-status-reward-used = Experiment complete. The technology is already researched.
fish-research-experiments-status-refunded = Experiment complete. Refunded { $points } points for this technology.
fish-research-experiments-status-unavailable = This server does not support the reward's research discipline.

fish-research-experiment-anomaly-survey-name = Anomaly catalog
fish-research-experiment-anomaly-survey-description = Scan { $required } different anomaly families. Variants of a rock anomaly count as one family.
fish-research-experiment-controlled-anomaly-name = Controlled anomaly
fish-research-experiment-controlled-anomaly-description = Scan an anomaly with at least { $severity }% severity, instability between { $minStability }% and { $maxStability }%, and at least { $health }% health.
fish-research-experiment-artifact-study-name = Investigated artifacts
fish-research-experiment-artifact-study-description = Scan { $required } different artifacts. Each must have at least { $nodes } unlocked nodes.
fish-research-experiment-biological-survey-name = Comparative physiology
fish-research-experiment-biological-survey-description = Measure { $required } different humanoid species. Subjects must be alive; repeated measurements of the same species do not count.
fish-research-experiment-power-cell-study-name = Power cell trials
fish-research-experiment-power-cell-study-description = Scan { $required } different power cell types. Each must have at least { $charge }% charge.
fish-research-experiment-robotics-fabrication-name = Applied robotics
fish-research-experiment-robotics-fabrication-description = Manufacture { $required } different pieces of robotics equipment. Repeating a recipe does not count.
fish-research-experiment-medical-fabrication-name = Medical equipment
fish-research-experiment-medical-fabrication-description = Manufacture { $required } different medical instruments. Repeating a recipe does not count.
fish-research-experiment-uranium-processing-name = Uranium processing
fish-research-experiment-uranium-processing-description = Produce { $required } units of processed uranium. Only finished output from a connected lathe counts.

